'''Plasmabeam''' is a [[Godly Weapons|godly]] gun that was originally obtainable by purchasing it individually from the [[Plasmabeam Gamepass]] for 1,699 Robux or from the [[Plasma Bundle]] for 3,399 Robux. It is now only obtainable through trading as the gamepasses have since went offsale.

== Appearance ==
It resembles an ancient colt pistol, but with a bulky silver frame. The barrel, attached to a portion of the frame and the cylinder, is long and thin in size with a small black muzzle. The cylinder is black with a small blue light on it. Above the barrel are three oval gaps, and by the hammer is an open circle. Connecting from the barrel and the trigger guard is a beam filled with plasma that has three semicircle indents, hence the name. The beam starts in a bright pink color, which then fades to a purplish color, and finally into a bright turquoise. The handle is black with a very dark purple handle that has a diamond-cut pattern over it.

==Trivia==
*It partners with the [[Godly Weapons|godly]] knife [[Plasmablade]], making the [https://murder-mystery-2.fandom.com/wiki/Murder_Mystery_2_Wiki:Wiki-Bot/Plasma_Set Plasma Set].
*This and its partner knife are the second gamepass weapons where you had the option to buy it as part of a bundle or separately, the first being [[Iceflake]] and [[Icebeam]].
*It was a victim of the [[The Duping Glitch (2022)|Duping Glitch (2022)]].
*It was designed by [[IDontHaveAUse]].

